Z||000006||Doni Hagan||08-29-2001||02:27 AM||||I just stumbled onto this thread and you're not lyin', V8!!<P>Around the 1st of August, I ordered a <BR>Konig Z-Racing gas cap door cover from Whitney via phone and was told by the "lady" that they were indeed in stock. I opted to paid for 2 day delivery. We're talkin' $22 for a $12 part. TEN DAYS LATER, I get an e-mail, mind you, stating that it was in fact OUT of stock and would be until the 1st of September. <BR>No mention of the $22 hurry-up-and-gimme-my-$#%t charge I paid. <P>After 2-3 phone calls I received a letter stating that the ENTIRE charge had been removed from my account. I HAD TO RE-ORDER THE THING. <P>I told them to ship it anyway they can figure out for $5. I miss the old Warsharski's store on State Street. You went there, showed the folks what you wanted and went outside to have a smoke. When you went back in, your part was there. Whitney was their mail-order division.   ||||reg||8
Z||000007||Haze_Performance||08-29-2001||03:38 AM||||They used to be in downtown Chicago. I've went there 100s of times. (Before they went mail order only) It was still a crappie operation then. They did have a few cool vintage cars displayed in there showroom.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR> <BR> <BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">          <BR></A>||||reg||10
